      ],
      "message": "wallet: guard null coin control in AvailableCoins TRUC filter\n\nAvailableCoins() takes an optional CCoinControl pointer that defaults to\nnullptr, and the other uses of it check for null first. The TRUC version\nfilter added in ec2676becd does not, so a call without coin control\ndereferences a null pointer as soon as the wallet has an unconfirmed\noutput in the mempool.\n\nNo current caller hits this: RPCs, the GUI and CreateTransaction always\npass a coin control, and the tests and benchmarks that use the default\nonly have confirmed coins.\n\nTreat a missing coin control like one that does not request a TRUC\ntransaction, and add a test that calls AvailableCoins() with the default\nargument on a wallet with an unconfirmed transaction.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Bruno Garcia",
        "email": "brunoely.gc@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T18:50:25Z"
      },
      "author": {
